failure_modes.text:
## 30. Product / system failure potential
For a visual demo, direct harm is low. Failure modes include:
- browser slowdown/high CPU;
- balls becoming visually unstable/overlapping;
- incorrect cursor interaction;
- partially offscreen initialization;
- timer throttling changing simulation behavior;
- deployment workflow never actually executing.

If the same collision code were reused for physically meaningful simulation, the lack of rigorous validation would become a much larger problem.

